@lang en
IMPORT `pti-tests-fixtures`

-- TESTS for Part 3: for each of the 32 exclusions, one fact pattern that triggers it and
-- one near miss that does not. A trigger asserts the whole list of exclusions that apply
-- (so that a second exclusion firing by accident would show); a near miss asserts that the
-- exclusion in question does not apply. The base case is a clean benefit-1 line for an
-- illness, admitted 1 March 2026, under the standard first-year policy. A failing
-- assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests — Part 3`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN it IS A `A claim item`
      p IS A `The insured person`
      pol IS A `The policy`
      e IS A `The event`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the case of` it `for` p `under` pol `for the event` e MEANS
    `the line` it `in` (`a claim by` p `under` pol `for` e `with the lines` (LIST it))

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance named in Part 3`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the clean line, arising from` cs MEANS
    `the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`) `and circumstances` cs `, and the standard stay`)

GIVEN ds IS A LIST OF `A condition named in the Rules`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the clean line, for` ds MEANS
    `the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` ds `and circumstances` EMPTY `, and the standard stay`)

GIVEN ts IS A LIST OF `A treatment named in the Rules`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the clean line, involving` ts MEANS
    `the case of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `(I) medicines used during the hospital stay` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000 `involving` ts) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` `the standard illness event`

GIVEN s IS A `The schedule`
      ts IS A LIST OF `A treatment named in the Rules`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the clean line, under` s `, involving` ts MEANS
    `the case of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `(I) medicines used during the hospital stay` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000 `involving` ts) `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a first-year policy on` s) `for the event` `the standard illness event`

GIVEN pl IS A `The place of treatment`
      s IS A `The schedule`
GIVETH AN `An item of a claim`
`the clean line, treated at` pl `, under` s MEANS
    `the case of` (`A claim item` WITH `the benefit` IS `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`, `the head of cost` IS `(I) medicines used during the hospital stay`, `the date` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the amount charged` IS 2_000_000, `the reasonable and customary amount` IS 2_000_000, `the treatments it involves` IS EMPTY, `the order` IS JUST `a licensed doctor`, `given during the hospital stay` IS TRUE, `the place of treatment` IS pl, `directly related to the illness or injury for which the insured person was then admitted` IS TRUE, `the insured person was in a critical condition threatening life and needing emergency treatment` IS FALSE, `the main benefit it belongs to` IS NOTHING, `the visit` IS 0, `a visit to one specialty of one medical establishment, with tests or diagnostics, a specific diagnosis and a doctor's order for treatment` IS TRUE, `the prescription was paid once already` IS FALSE) `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a first-year policy on` s) `for the event` `the standard illness event`

-- An illness event with one of the fields the general constructor leaves at its default.
GIVEN sport IS A MAYBE `A sporting activity`
      death IS A MAYBE DATE
      unknown IS A BOOLEAN
      surgery IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The event`
`the standard illness, with sport` sport `, death` death `, cause of death unknown:` unknown `, surgery first ordered` surgery MEANS
    `The event` WITH
        `the cause`                                IS `an illness`
        `the accident`                             IS NOTHING
        `the illness`                              IS JUST `the standard illness`
        `the conditions diagnosed`                 IS LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`
        `the circumstances`                        IS EMPTY
        `the sporting activity`                    IS sport
        `the hospital stay`                        IS JUST `the standard stay`
        `the date of death`                        IS death
        `the cause of death unknown`               IS unknown
        `the disablement`                          IS NOTHING
        `the date the surgery was first ordered`   IS surgery
        `the date of the outpatient diagnosis`     IS NOTHING

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of sport or activity`
      km IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sporting activity`
`competing in` k `at` km `km from the shore` MEANS
    `A sporting activity` WITH
        `the kind`                                              IS k
        `distance from the shore, in km`                        IS km
        `a charity race`                                        IS FALSE
        `a race organised internally by a company`              IS FALSE
        `the insured person's main and regular source of income` IS FALSE
        `training or competing`                                 IS TRUE

`a birth event` MEANS
    `an event: cause` `pregnancy or childbirth` `, accident` NOTHING `, illness` NOTHING `, diagnoses` EMPTY `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` (JUST `the standard stay`)

§§ `The clean case`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Exclusions 1-7: causes`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `an intentional act of a legal heir of the insured person`)) EQUALS LIST 1
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `an intentional act of the insured person`)) EQUALS LIST 1
-- Exclusion 2: a traffic offence at 14 (born 1 January 2012; the event is on 1 March 2026)
-- is excluded; at 13 (born 1 June 2012) it is not; a breach of other law is, at any age.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` (`a person born on` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`) `and circumstances` (LIST `a breach of traffic law by the insured person`) `, and the standard stay`)) EQUALS LIST 2
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 2 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` (`a person born on` (YMD 2012 6 1)) `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`) `and circumstances` (LIST `a breach of traffic law by the insured person`) `, and the standard stay`)))
#ASSERT `exclusion 2 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` (`a person born on` (YMD 2012 6 1)) `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`) `and circumstances` (LIST `a breach of the law, or of rules of the local authority, by the insured person`) `, and the standard stay`))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `the insured person being under the influence of alcohol, beer or another stimulant`)) EQUALS LIST 3
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 3 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 4: fighting, unless proven to be solely in self-defence.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `the insured person fighting`)) EQUALS LIST 4
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 4 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `the insured person fighting`, `proof that the fighting was solely in self-defence`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `a volcanic eruption`)) EQUALS LIST 5
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 5 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` EMPTY))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `a strike`)) EQUALS LIST 6
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 6 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 7: aviation, but not as a ticketed passenger.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `taking part in aviation`)) EQUALS LIST 7
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 7 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `taking part in aviation as a passenger holding a ticket`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `taking part in military training exercises`)) EQUALS LIST 7
-- Two causes at once.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `the insured person being under the influence of alcohol, beer or another stimulant`, `the insured person fighting`)) EQUALS LIST 3, 4

§§ `Exclusions 8-11`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `malaria`)) EQUALS LIST 8
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 8 applies to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`)))
-- Exclusion 9: functional food is excluded; a vaccination in newborn care is not.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a functional food`)) EQUALS LIST 9
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a vaccination`)) EQUALS LIST 9
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 9 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `benefit 4: newborn care` `for` `vaccination` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 1_000_000 `involving` (LIST `a vaccination`)) `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) `for the event` `a birth event`))
-- Exclusion 10: at a convalescent home; not home nursing at home.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, treated at` `a convalescent home in Vietnam` `, under` `the full schedule`) EQUALS LIST 10
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 10 applies to` (`the case of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: home nursing` `for` `hiring a nurse` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `the insured person's home in Vietnam` `, ordered by` (JUST `a licensed doctor`)) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` `the standard illness event`))
#ASSERT `exclusion 10 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `treatment at home that is not a home nursing service`))
-- Exclusion 11: stress, yes; an acute mental disorder that ends once stabilised, no.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `stress`)) EQUALS LIST 11
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 11 applies to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `an acute mental disorder whose symptoms end once treatment stabilises it`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `treatment for the premenopause`)) EQUALS LIST 11

§§ `Exclusion 12`
-- Surgery first ordered on 1 November 2025, before the start date of 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` NOTHING `, death` NOTHING `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` (JUST (YMD 2025 11 1)))) EQUALS LIST 12
-- Not where the contract is extended to pre-existing conditions.
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 12 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a first-year policy on` `the full schedule, extended for pre-existing conditions`) `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` NOTHING `, death` NOTHING `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` (JUST (YMD 2025 11 1)))))
-- Ordered on the start date itself: not before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 12 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` NOTHING `, death` NOTHING `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)))))
-- The medical costs of an accident on 15 December 2025, before the start date.
#ASSERT `exclusion 12 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 1 5) `of` 2_000_000) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an event: cause` `an accident` `, accident` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2025 12 15) `of the kind` `an accident in daily life`)) `, illness` NOTHING `, diagnoses` EMPTY `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` NOTHING))
-- The same accident, on a policy renewed continuously since 2023 (fork F3): not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 12 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 1 5) `of` 2_000_000) `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) `for the event` (`an event: cause` `an accident` `, accident` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2025 12 15) `of the kind` `an accident in daily life`)) `, illness` NOTHING `, diagnoses` EMPTY `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` NOTHING)))

§§ `Exclusions 13-16`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `assisted reproduction, such as in-vitro fertilisation`)) EQUALS LIST 13
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 13 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 14: pregnancy without the maternity benefit; not with it.
#ASSERT `exclusion 14 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `benefit 4: maternity care` `for` `a normal delivery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 10_000_000) `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a first-year policy on` `the full schedule without maternity cover`) `for the event` `a birth event`)
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 14 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `benefit 4: maternity care` `for` `a normal delivery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 10_000_000) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` `a birth event`))
-- Exclusion 15: a routine eyesight test; not a gynaecological examination to treat a disease.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a routine eyesight test`)) EQUALS LIST 15
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 15 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a gynaecological or andrological examination or test to treat a disease`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a caesarean section at the request of the insured person or their representative`)) EQUALS LIST 16
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 16 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` EMPTY))

§§ `Exclusions 17-22`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `orthopaedic correction or rehabilitation that does not follow on from treatment of an illness`)) EQUALS LIST 17
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 17 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 18: buying an aid; not surgery to replace one.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `buying, maintaining, repairing or replacing a prosthesis or an aid`)) EQUALS LIST 18
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 18 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `surgery to maintain, repair or replace a prosthesis or an aid`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `a dietary supplement or substitute, natural and sold without prescription`)) EQUALS LIST 19
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 19 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 20: cataract surgery, unless the contract is extended to special diseases.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `cataract surgery`)) EQUALS LIST 20
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 20 applies to` (`the clean line, under` `the full schedule, extended for special diseases` `, involving` (LIST `cataract surgery`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `surgery to restore sight`)) EQUALS LIST 20
-- Exclusion 21: cosmetic surgery; not reconstruction after an accident in the period.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `cosmetic treatment or surgery`)) EQUALS LIST 21
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 21 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `reconstruction, ordered by a doctor, of an organ injured in an accident in the period of insurance`)))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, involving` (LIST `treatment to control body weight`)) EQUALS LIST 22
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 22 applies to` (`the clean line, involving` EMPTY))

§§ `Exclusions 23-26`
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `phimosis`)) EQUALS LIST 23
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 23 applies to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`)))
-- Exclusion 24: competing in hunting (a dangerous sport); not sailing 5 km from the shore.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` (JUST (`competing in` `hunting` `at` 0 `km from the shore`)) `, death` NOTHING `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` NOTHING)) EQUALS LIST 24
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 24 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` (JUST (`competing in` `sailing` `at` 5 `km from the shore`)) `, death` NOTHING `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` NOTHING)))
-- Exclusion 25: dental treatment without the dental benefit; not with it; not emergency
-- dental treatment after an accident.
#ASSERT `exclusion 25 applies to` (`the clean line, under` `the full schedule without dental cover` `, involving` (LIST `dental treatment`))
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 25 applies to` (`the clean line, under` `the full schedule` `, involving` (LIST `dental treatment`)))
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 25 applies to` (`the clean line, under` `the full schedule without dental cover` `, involving` (LIST `emergency dental treatment because of an accident`)))
-- Exclusion 26: hepatitis (a special disease) in the first year; not after it.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `hepatitis`)) EQUALS LIST 26
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 26 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`) `for the event` (`an illness, with diagnoses` (LIST `hepatitis`) `and circumstances` EMPTY `, and the standard stay`)))
-- A pre-existing illness (symptoms known in November 2025) in the first year.
#ASSERT `exclusion 26 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an event: cause` `an illness` `, accident` NOTHING `, illness` (JUST (`The illness` WITH `the date it began` IS YMD 2025 10 1, `where it arose` IS `Vietnam`, `dates on which it was treated before` IS EMPTY, `the date the insured person first knew of its symptoms or of the illness` IS JUST (YMD 2025 11 1), `its marks` IS EMPTY, `a competent authority has given a clear conclusion on the pathology` IS TRUE, `the direct cause of the death or the disablement` IS TRUE)) `, diagnoses` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`) `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` (JUST `the standard stay`)))

§§ `Exclusions 27-32`
-- Exclusion 27: 26 hours in hospital without admission is a hospitalisation (definition 31)
-- but not inpatient treatment (definition 32): outpatient treatment, excluded without the
-- outpatient benefit and not with it.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` (`a first-year policy on` `the full schedule without outpatient cover`) `for the event` (`an illness, with the stay` (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 2) `, hours` 26 `, admitted` FALSE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a hospital in Vietnam`))) EQUALS LIST 27
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 27 applies to` (`the case of` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`an illness, with the stay` (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 2) `, hours` 26 `, admitted` FALSE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a hospital in Vietnam`))))
-- Exclusion 28: treated in another Asian country without the extension; not with it.
#ASSERT `exclusion 28 applies to` (`the clean line, treated at` `a hospital in another Asian country` `, under` `the full schedule`)
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 28 applies to` (`the clean line, treated at` `a hospital in another Asian country` `, under` `the full schedule, extended to Asia`))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `an epidemic risk announced by a competent authority`)) EQUALS LIST 29
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 29 applies to` (`the clean line, arising from` EMPTY))
-- Exclusion 30: the scalpel in Longo surgery; not other consumables.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `consumables` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 4_000_000 `involving` (LIST `the scalpel used in Longo haemorrhoid surgery`)) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` `the standard illness event`) EQUALS LIST 30
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 30 applies to` (`the case of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `consumables` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 4_000_000) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` `the standard illness event`))
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `high liver enzymes`)) EQUALS LIST 31
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 31 applies to` (`the clean line, for` (LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`)))
-- Exclusion 32: death of unknown cause; not when the cause is known.
#ASSERT `the exclusions of Part 3 that apply to` (`the case of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `benefit 6: death from illness` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` NOTHING `, death` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, cause of death unknown:` TRUE `, surgery first ordered` NOTHING)) EQUALS LIST 32
#ASSERT NOT (`exclusion 32 applies to` (`the case of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `benefit 6: death from illness` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `for` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for the event` (`the standard illness, with sport` NOTHING `, death` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, cause of death unknown:` FALSE `, surgery first ordered` NOTHING)))

§§ `An exclusion reaches the outcome`
#ASSERT `the outcome for` (`the clean line, arising from` (LIST `terrorism`)) `, given what was counted before:` EMPTY EQUALS `excluded` (LIST 6)
